Boot-arg metal_ubwc_rt=1: CoreAnimation's offscreen render targets compressed (UBWC), 2026-11-12, darwin-lisa session 9.

Private and memoryless render targets of RGBA8, BGRA8 or RGBA16Float, one 2D level, 256x256 pixels or more, not
written by a kernel and not to be viewed in another format, are made with hakios_metal_texture_new_compressed (the
core's hakios-metal-x-ubwc-rt.patch: cleared, drawn into, sampled, fetched and copied out compressed). Those are the
glass's backdrops (1088x2432 BGRA8 and RGBA16Float, 576x1216 RGBA16Float), its blur levels and the layers
CoreAnimation flattens. Linear, each full-screen read of one costs the texture unit some 0.85 ms (probe "full-screen
cost": a fetch over the screen 1.78 ms a draw against 0.93 without) and each Clear of a 1088x2432 RGBA16Float one some
1.8 ms (21 MB at the 12 GB/s measured); compressed, a Clear writes a few bytes a block and flat UI content moves a
fraction of its bytes. Off unless asked: the layout is drawn into on the phone for the first time with it. A texture
the core will not compress is made linear as before. metal_noubwc turns this off too. With metal_fps=timeline each
one made is named ("timeline: a compressed render target of ...").

